				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 09 Aug 2019 00:23:20 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>LordSpy</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1977151</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>The escalation is a bit slow at first, but it gets gloriously contrived by the end. Also, the interview is fantastic, though it takes a bit of internal handwaving to excuse the parentheses and '‽' signs being there from a spoken transcript, but hey, it's a -J so that is 110% excused.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-7210132#post-4257902</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-7210132/scp-2002-j#post-4257902</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 22 May 2019 20:53:12 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Quinson</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3357681</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>When I first started reading it the first thought to go through my mind was, &quot;Why in the actual hell does something like this exist, this scp is going to be dumb&quot; and when I saw the amount of upvotes it had I was confused. So I continued to read it and was struct with an absolute goldmine of a story.<br /> I never expected it to start/end/continue/etc like this. But honestly I relate way to much to this guy, I would end up selling my soul for something as stupid as this, maybe not completely slowing down at an intersection would be my deal with the demon (Sine it's technically illegal)</p> <p>+1</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
